    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="0646" n="570" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg570"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">660M.116/9: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Lithuania</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kuykendall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-07-19T16:00:00-04:00">July 19, 1935—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. Your despatch No. 266 of June 22, 1935.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d459-f1"/>
                    Please request in writing Lithuanian Foreign Office to furnish Legation with a
                    statement covering attitude of Lithuanian Government towards imports of
                    petroleum products from the United States and the policy that Lithuania intends
                    to pursue with respect to the issuance of import licenses covering such
                    products. Forward report by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
